        "last_edited_date": 1748460436000,
        "comments": "An EF-0 tornado touched down on the east side of the City of Columbia at the intersection of Columbia Purvis Road and US Highway 98. The initial damage started at Beacon Hardware Supply with roof damage. The tornado then moved northeast through the Lakeview community. The tornado caused minor roof damage to numerous homes, scattered tree damage, and collapsed a few unattached sheds. The tornado ended in the woods just northeast of Lakeview Drive. Peak winds were estimated to be 85 mph with a peak width of 75 yards for the nearly 2 mile track.",
